1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:06,911
I just got back from a trip to LA. I've been traveling a lot lately, and while it's been fun I'm very happy to be home.
我刚从洛杉矶回来。最近旅行很多，虽然很开心，但回到家也很高兴。

2
00:00:06,921 --> 00:00:11,601
While I was there, I met up with a new creator friend, Megan Tan, in person for the first time ever.
在那里，我第一次在线下见到了新认识的创作者朋友 Megan Tan。

3
00:00:11,601 --> 00:00:17,271
It was such an adventure, and I think we had an even better time than we thought we would.
那是一次很棒的经历，甚至比预想的还开心。

4
00:00:17,281 --> 00:00:22,360
Today I want to talk about the one mindset shift that completely changed my 20s.
今天想聊一个改变我二十多岁生活方式的想法。

5
00:00:22,360 --> 00:00:27,841
For the past several years I've had this personal motto that goes, say yes now, figure it out later.
过去几年，我有句自己的座右铭：先答应尝试，办法之后再想。

6
00:00:27,841 --> 00:00:36,201
I've talked about it once on here before, and it is a motto that I hold very close to my heart and has been responsible for many events in my life.
以前在这里提过一次。这句话对我很重要，也促成了不少经历。

7
00:00:36,201 --> 00:00:42,600
It's my little tattoo on my wrist, and I cannot believe it's already been 2 years since I got this thing. That's crazy.
我还把它纹在手腕上，没想到已经两年了，时间真快。

8
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:51,920
A lot has changed since then, and I always find it very interesting to revisit themes at different phases in my life and see if it's still relevant.
后来改变了很多，我很喜欢在不同人生阶段重看旧想法，看看是否还适用。

9
00:00:51,920 --> 00:01:03,960
If things have changed or if it's reinforced, and for this in particular there have been a few things that have reminded me of it.
有些想法会变，有些会更坚定；最近也有几件事让我再次想起这句话。

10
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:13,401
When I had first come up with the phrase figure it out later, it was after I had dropped out of college and was slowly finding my way in the world.
最初想到这句话时，我刚离开大学，正慢慢探索自己的路。

11
00:01:13,401 --> 00:01:17,880
I had an idea of what I wanted to do, but I wasn't great at putting myself out there.
我大概知道想做什么，但不太擅长主动展示自己、去接触机会。

12
00:01:17,880 --> 00:01:26,761
I cared way too much about what people thought. I was way too in my head about some things, and I struggled to really find my voice.
我太在意别人的看法，也容易想太多，很难找到自己的表达。

13
00:01:26,761 --> 00:01:30,081
And throughout this time, figure it out was my anchor.
那段时间，想办法这句话像一个支点。

14
00:01:30,081 --> 00:01:35,881
It was a way of reminding myself to just make a decision, and I will figure it out when I get there.
它提醒我先做出选择，走到那一步再想办法。

15
00:01:35,881 --> 00:01:40,281
Sort of having this trust in yourself while taking these leaps of faith.
就是在迈出未知的一步时，保留一点对自己的信任。

16
00:01:40,281 --> 00:01:43,561
And periodically it will pop in and out of my life.
这个想法也会时不时在生活中重新出现。

17
00:01:43,561 --> 00:01:50,001
I think we inherently know when we connect with the idea of something. It feels exciting and terrifying all at once.
我觉得，当一个想法真正吸引自己时，会同时感到兴奋和害怕。

18
00:01:50,001 --> 00:01:56,521
But before we even have the chance to pursue it, we often hold ourselves back because we don't know how it will turn out.
还没真正尝试，就可能因为不知道结果而退缩。

19
00:01:56,521 --> 00:02:03,081
When Megan asked me to go on a trip to the West Coast, there was a moment where I felt hesitant to go.
Megan 邀我去西海岸旅行时，我有一瞬间很犹豫。

20
00:02:03,081 --> 00:02:09,801
It had been a while since I've done anything like that. We had only just begun to know each other, and I was considering saying no.
我已经有阵子没这样旅行了，彼此也刚开始熟悉，所以考虑过拒绝。

21
00:02:09,801 --> 00:02:16,481
But you never know what an opportunity will lead to, and you never know how impactful something will be till after you've done it.
但有时，只有尝试之后，才知道一个机会会带来怎样的经历。

22
00:02:16,481 --> 00:02:22,521
There could be a million different things that could make it the wrong choice, but you only need a few good reasons for it to be right.
你可以想出无数顾虑，也可能找到几个值得尝试的理由。

23
00:02:22,561 --> 00:02:28,361
There was a period of my life where I was feeling very stagnant. I wasn't meeting new people or experiencing new things.
有一阵子，我感觉生活停滞了，没有认识新人，也没体验新事物。

24
00:02:28,361 --> 00:02:31,281
But I was also not putting myself out there at the same time.
但那时，我自己也没有主动迈出去。

25
00:02:31,321 --> 00:02:36,920
But I think it's also important not to take it too far, and it's not about saying yes to everything.
不过我也觉得，不该把这个想法推得太远，不是所有事都要答应。

26
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:40,640
But it's important to know when something will be a healthy push.
要分辨什么时候一次尝试能适当地推动自己。

27
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:47,041
It can be intimidating to open yourself up, to show the world who you are and not know how it's going to be received.
展示真实的自己，又不知道别人会怎么回应，确实会让人紧张。

28
00:02:47,081 --> 00:02:55,920
But we're never going to know what's on the other side unless we're willing to take that first step and see where that tells us where to go next.
如果不愿迈出第一步，就很难知道另一边有什么，也无法从经历中找到下一步方向。

29
00:02:55,920 --> 00:03:02,921
The beauty of putting yourself out there is that it also forces you to be adapted and creative in ways you may have not expected.
主动尝试的好处是，也会迫使你用没想到的方式调整和创造。

30
00:03:03,840 --> 00:03:14,361
C, it opens you up to seeing things in a different way, learning from different people and maybe even finding things you weren't even looking for.
它让你从不同角度看事情，向不同的人学习，甚至遇到意想不到的收获。

31
00:03:14,361 --> 00:03:21,241
There will always be some level of risk involved when it comes to doing something completely out of the ordinary from what we're used to.
做完全超出日常习惯的事情，总会有某种不确定性。

32
00:03:21,241 --> 00:03:23,791
But honestly I think that's just the name of the game.
不过，我觉得这也是尝试新事物时难免的一部分。

33
00:03:23,801 --> 00:03:30,681
And depending on what season of life we're in, it's either going to be a yes or no, and I think both and answers are valid.
不同人生阶段会有不同答案，答应或拒绝都可以。

34
00:03:30,681 --> 00:03:48,000
It depends just where you're at in life. And if it's a yes then sometimes it'll work and sometimes it won't, but either way you'll learn something from it.
取决于自己当下的状态。答应尝试后，有时顺利、有时不顺，但无论如何都能有所学习。
